<!--
  Chapter 75 — Multi-Tenancy, Multi-Region & Compliance.
    tenancy/   Cluster (a throwaway PostgreSQL 16), TenancyModel (shared table + RLS, schema per tenant, database per
               tenant), TenantScope (the tenant set per transaction, so pooled connections can't leak it)
    erasure/   CryptoShredder (per-subject AES-GCM keys in a separate store), ByteScan (where erased bytes survive)
  verify/run.sh compares the three models, provokes tenant leaks, measures a noisy neighbour and traces an erasure.
-->
